  "notes": "Verse + chorus (16 bars of 2/4 eighths in the source) written as 16 bars of 4/4 quarters, transposed G->C. No pickup. Old version was wrong: it dropped the low G3/B3 notes (bar 2 ended on a D half, bar 4 had C + rest) and replaced the chorus with an invented tune. Chorus dotted figures (E>F) simplified to even quarters for the level. Range issue: in C the chorus dips to F3/E3 (MIDI 53/52), below the elementary RH floor 55; in G major (keyFifths 1) the whole tune would fit B3-C5. LH: single roots C3/G2, F chord voiced as A2 (F/A) to stay inside LH range 43-62. Transposed from C to G major so the low chorus stays within the level range."
